{title: Dwelling in Beulah Land}
{artist: C. Austin Miles}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
[G]Far away the noise of strife upon my ear is falling;
[C]then I know the sins of earth beset on [G]every hand.
Doubt and fear and things of earth in vain to me are calling —
[A]none of these shall move me from Beulah [D]Land.

Chorus
I'm [G]living on the mountain, underneath a cloudless [C]sky —
I'm [G]drinking at the fountain that never shall run [D]dry;
O [G]yes, I'm feasting on the manna from a bountiful sup[C]ply,
for [G]I am dwelling in [D]Beulah [G]Land!
